    "body": "If users withdraw their consent to store data, information should be stored to report about it so the admin knows it happened, from whom (although this is arguably an issue) and when.\r\n\r\nStoring this info in track_e_default should be enough to generate the report afterwards.\r\n\r\nThe report should available in a new \"Personal Data Privacy\" block on the admin page.\r\n\r\nThe interface should also receive \"requests for erasure\" (right to be forgotten) and enable the admin to take action (with e-mail reminders because it cannot take longer than a month).\r\n\r\nParticularly specific information about the right to be forgotten available here: https://ico.org.uk/for-organisations/guide-to-the-general-data-protection-regulation-gdpr/individual-rights/right-to-erasure/\r\nOur admin page should point there or to the closest equivalent on the EU website to allow for the admin to be informed before taking a decision.",
